{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>יְהוּדָה אַתָּה, etc.</b> — One needs to know why it was necessary to say <b>אַתָּה</b>, since he was speaking with him right there, and what does it come to limit? Further, why did he not say ״וְיָדְכָה״ etc. and ״יִשְׁתַּחֲווּ״ etc., since these are additional matters?" "<b>And it appears</b> that the verse's intent is along this path: <b>אַתָּה יוֹדוּךָ</b> — meaning, the sovereignty does not begin in the future in the manner of the other blessings spoken to the rest of the brothers, which are for distant times, when they enter the land; rather, you yourself — your brothers praise you. And so it says in Divrei HaYamim (1 Chronicles 5:2): ״יְהוּדָה גָּבַר בְּאֶחָיו״. And when the time comes that your hand is on the neck of your enemies and you prevail over the enemies, then they shall bow down to you etc., and they shall make you king over them. And this was in the days of Saul, when David achieved the great victory over the neck of his enemies — Israel made him king over them."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:50:28.052262388Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}